    <string name="whitelist_help_title">Whitelist paths</string>
    <string name="whitelist_help">Whitelist paths apply to this rule. Other rules can still clean these paths; set the whitelist in each overlapping rule. Paths start from “In folder”. Case sensitivity follows the filesystem; aliases of the same protected item are also kept.\n\nFor example, in %1$s:\n\nkeep → %2$s\nKeeps this item and all its contents.\n\nimages/photo.jpg → %3$s\nKeeps this file.\n\nPaths match exactly. *, ? and [] are literal characters. keep does not match sub/keep or keeper.\n\nWhen deleting whole folders, a target that contains a protected path is kept in its entirety, even if that path does not exist yet.</string>
